            "review_title": "Review at Hanayuki",
            "review_text": "Hoai Thu Hofstetter\nThun, Switzerland53 contributions\n0\nFresh sushi taste in Saigon\nNov 2015 • Friends\nHanayuki is my one and only pleasing place for sushi in Saigon. Usually ordered salmon/tuna sashimi together with sushi rolls and favorite Japanese pancake (Bánh xèo Nhật). The things I love about Hanayuki is their seafood are always fresh in taste and flavour. Plus, I get personal server anytime dining here and they never disappoint me. My referable drinks are hot green tea and lemon iced soda. End of the meal, continually get a complimentary fruit-of-the-day as dessert. \n\nHanayuki has also large rooms for groups and families with on-ground seats as Japanese traditional style. The price is a bit high-end class but compare with what you receive - service and food quality - totally reasonable. You would pay about 800,000 to 1,000,000 VND for 2 people per meal here ( without beer and alcohol).\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten April 9, 2016",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-14",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
        },
