            "review_text": "gidzmmo\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam31 contributions\n0\nGreat food, fresh fish, good value\nFeb 2016 • Solo\nThis is my regular Japanese restaurant. Portions are large and prices reasonable. Fish is always fresh, so the sashimi and sushi are excellent. They also do tasty hot pots and shabu shabu. Set lunch menus are good value for money and you do get quite a lot of food.\n\nMy favourite orders from Hanayuki: Sashimi Moriawase and Sake Don (very generous with the salmon slices), hot plate liver, shabu shabu.\n\nI love that they always give complimentary dessert (usually fresh fruit or sometime homemade yoghurt).\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten February 19, 2016",
