            "review_title": "Review at Hanayuki",
            "review_text": "katanankes\nHo Chi Minh City, Vietnam90 contributions\n0\nFinally some good sushi in Saigon\nApr 2015 • Solo\nRecently I have been wandering around Saigon looking for new Japanese restaurants, something beyond the usual \"Bars\" and \"Delis\". I found some good ones, but quite expensive. Finding a restaurant that combine excellent Japanese food and reasonable prices was a great positive surprise. By the way, the place is just next to a very famous sushi place located on Le Thanh Ton 1, but it is way superior in my opinion. \n\nI stumbled upon Hanayuki for an early dinner. The staff hardly speaks any English, but they are friendly and ordering is quite easy thanks to an extensive visually enriched menu. \n\nIn Saigon sushi tend to be a bit \"shallow\" in my opinion. It lacks the freshness and the tasty flavor of real Japanese sushi... The one that I ate at Hanayuki is a pleasant exception to the rule. The sashimi was excellent and very fresh and as an added bonus they have some sushi specialties that you do not easily find elsewhere, such as rolls with fried salmon skin. They have an extensive choice of Japanese street dishes that I did not have time to try (been there only twice since my discovery). \n\nI look forward to going back!\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten April 10, 2015",
